	(text_box "Module utilises the X and Y count from the PositionCounters module to define a viewport within the frame\n\nThe default is a 320x200 window that comfortably fits both NTSC and PAL timing retaining an unused border around the viewport.\n\nThe viewport size can be redefined by changing the start and end triggers up to the limits of the full frame, less the sync and backporch/frontporch portion of the timing (see FrameTiming)\n\nThe PAL timing assumes that 50 extra lines of video are generated, this transforms the default 60Hz frame into 50Hz and adds to the border above and below the viewport\n\nThe mechanism is to use simple, minimal astable latches to turn the viewport signals on and off. The danger is that the \"on\" pattern being tested for will repeat after the \"off\" signal so care must be taken to ensure that the matching logic tests for 0s not just 1s"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 137.16 19.05 0)
		(size 66.04 45.72)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
